{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q6119792","formula":"C₃₆H₅₂ClMnN₂O₂","hill":"C36H52ClMnN2O2","elements":["H","C","N","O","Cl","Mn"],"composition":{"C":36.0,"H":52.0,"N":2.0,"O":2.0,"Cl":1.0,"Mn":1.0},"names":{"en":"Jacobsen's catalyst"},"descriptions":{"en":"Jacobsen's catalyst is the common name for N,N'-bis(3,5-di-tert-butylsalicylidene)-1,2-cyclohexane­diaminomanganese(III) chloride, a coordination compound of manganese and a salen-type ligand. It is used as an asymmetric catalyst in the Jacobsen epoxidation, which is renowned for its ability to enantioselectively transform prochiral alkenes into epoxides. Before its development, catalysts for the asymmetric epoxidation of alkenes required the substrate to have a directing functional group, such as an alcohol as seen in the Sharpless epoxidation."},"fame":9,"pubchemCid":73602790,"mass":635.2,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC(C)(C)C1=CC(=C(C(=C1)C(C)(C)C)[O-])C=N[C@@H]2CCCC[C@H]2N=CC3=C(C(=CC(=C3)C(C)(C)C)C(C)(C)C)[O-].[Cl-].[Mn+3]","inchikey":"LJVAWOSDJSQANR-SEILFYAJSA-K","iupac":"2,4-ditert-butyl-6-[[(1R,2R)-2-[(3,5-ditert-butyl-2-oxidophenyl)methylideneamino]cyclohexyl]iminomethyl]phenolate;manganese(3+);chloride","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"73602790","atoms":94,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":5.928,"y":1.361,"z":3.021,"el":"C"},{"x":6.604,"y":1.671,"z":1.664,"el":"C"},{"x":8.128,"y":1.516,"z":1.874,"el":"C"},{"x":6.343,"y":3.146,"z":1.292,"el":"C"},{"x":6.028,"y":0.759,"z":0.569,"el":"C"},{"x":4.658,"y":0.736,"z":0.317,"el":"C"},{"x":4.1,"y":-0.078,"z":-0.69,"el":"C"},{"x":4.881,"y":-0.94,"z":-1.52,"el":"C"},{"x":6.294,"y":-0.928,"z":-1.253,"el":"C"},{"x":6.814,"y":-0.081,"z":-0.227,"el":"C"},{"x":7.296,"y":-1.837,"z":-2.053,"el":"C"},{"x":6.959,"y":-3.333,"z":-1.847,"el":"C"},{"